// A planted map for BRIDGES (profile 1.15, after the parallel-pass trial of 30 Sep 2026): a step
// that is a premise of a named causal scheme, so the state the chain stops at is taken on by the
// argument rather than left as a gap; a second bridge whose premises state no step, which bridges
// nothing; and a state the chain stops at that nothing argues from -- a gap still.
===
title: "Bridges -- a planted mechanism in an argument"
mechanism:
    question: "What does a curfew do to the town?"
    levels: [town, people]
    actors:
        council: {label: "The council", level: town}
        youth:   {label: "Young people", level: people}
    states:
        curfew:  {label: "The council imposes a curfew", actor: council, role: intervention}
        crime:   {label: "Night-time crime", actor: youth, role: outcome}
        resent:  {label: "Young people resent the council", actor: youth}
        trust:   {label: "Trust in the council", actor: youth}
        graffiti: {label: "Graffiti on the council offices", actor: youth}
===

[Keep the curfew]: The council should keep the curfew.

<The curfew's consequences>

(1) [The curfew cuts crime]: The curfew cuts night-time crime.
    {causes: {from: curfew, to: crime, sign: "-", basis: asserted}}
(2) [Less crime is good]: Less night-time crime is good for the town.
-- From consequences {uses: [1, 2]} --
(3) [Keep the curfew]

<Nothing causal here>

(1) [The council voted for it]: The council voted for the curfew.
-- From a mechanism to what to do {uses: [1]} --
(2) [The vote binds]: The vote binds the council.
    +> [Keep the curfew]

<The curfew costs trust>

(1) [The curfew breeds resentment]: The curfew breeds resentment.
    {causes: {from: curfew, to: resent, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}
(2) [Resentment wears trust away]: Resentment wears trust in the council away.
    {causes: {from: resent, to: trust, sign: "-", basis: asserted}}
-- From cause to effect {uses: [1, 2]} --
(3) [The curfew costs the council trust]: The curfew costs the council the young people's trust.
    -> [Keep the curfew]

[Resentment shows on the walls]: Resentment shows as graffiti on the council offices.
    {causes: {from: resent, to: graffiti, sign: "+", basis: asserted}}
